Bug: CU reparse leaves behind a header declaration it no longer emits

source.c defines FEATURE before it includes header.h, so parsing it adds the
declaration of feature_only at header.h:2. When source.c is changed on disk to no
longer define FEATURE and is parsed again, that declaration stays in the table.

Cause: building a CU's knowledge removes only the references positioned in the CU.
header.h did not change, so nothing removes its references. Under ADR-0032 nothing
may, since other includers could have added the same ones (all or nothing).

Fix: ADR-0033. Every CU reaching header.h, here only source.c, has parsed since the
declaration was last added, so the sweep removes it. Item sweep in doc/backlog.md
takes this test off suspension.
